                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Still my favorite RPG Maker game years later.\n\nThe gameplay is about what you'd expect from a solid RPG (though it does spice it up with punishing choices to make), but every other aspect of the game, from the story to the music, elevates it to something truly great.\n\nWhile games like Yakuza balance serious & silly by effortlessly intertwining them, LISA keeps them on opposite ends and relishes in the whiplash you'll get from switching between them.\n\nIt's a game that's as joyful as it is oppressive, a fantastic experience all around.",
